C2 single-Admission Target recovery orchestration
Date: 2026-10-07
Base: main@5df8775bc38839add7e3087d70155e7bcf672aa6; this base remains local pending publication.

TargetPublishRecoveryExecutor has no Journal/Producer/physical publication dependency. It reads guarded retained work once, signs the recovery UNKNOWN once, retains the exact mutation before queue submission and retries only that handoff. A pending different Admission/Owner is rejected. Exact APPLIED Source first result with the recovery code/hash is required to clear its local slot. It does not authorize historical/terminal resolution or a first send.

Local development command:
./gradlew test --tests 'com.nereusstream.delay.runtime.TargetCommandStoreTest.modifiesActualTimelineOrClaimWithHistoryAndFirstResults' checkstyleMain checkstyleTest --no-daemon --console=plain
Result: 19/19 tests, zero failure/error/skip; main style passed. Combined build failed on one formatting-only test line (then wrapped). Previous fixture failure correctly rejected binding the same SharedRocksDbResources to a second WorkClass registry; the replacement now reuses the actual single Worker graph.

The new local scenario applies a v4 Admission, pauses/closes the old Worker source, releases its lease, acquires a higher epoch, reopens/audits the actual format-2 root and activates that epoch before composing the new Worker. Ordinary first-send read of the old Admission is rejected, while recovery signs under the new Owner. Queued duplicate handoff makes one fixture source append; Source applies UNKNOWN, keeps original Owner epoch in its obligation, exact reserve/allocated and execution charge, and keeps strict barrier without ORDER_HEAD. ACK_UNKNOWN retries only ACK, without another Store write or authority resolution; exact Source proof settles the local recovery slot. Stale old lease cannot release the new Owner.

The same scenario is exposed as an opt-in real-service test using two Oxia ClientHandles with different session-derived identities and a unique owned prefix. e2e/run-oxia-real-service.sh includes it. Source append/consumer, historical keys/config and logical clock remain fixtures even when the lease CAS uses the real service. No real Broker, process crash, new Store incarnation install or production certification is implied. Bounded recovered-work enumeration/history resolver, Host lifecycle, all remaining evidence branches, checkpoint/Floor/GC and full 29-slice verification remain required.

Final real-service command and scope are recorded in c2-target-publish-recovery-oxia-real.log: one real Oxia test passes, zero failure/error/skip; main/test Checkstyle passes. The new test uses the same actual Worker resource graph with two connected native sessions. A previous native attempt exposed a valid transient Host admission-busy refusal before the fixture's first drain; the fixture now uses the existing bounded awaitShardAdmission plus a 10-second overall retry bound for only that exact refusal. Production busy guards and completion assertions are unchanged. The final native test exercises this updated fixture; local 19-case report precedes that fixture-only wait adjustment.
